+# BLUE CURRENT V50.30.0 — V50 RELEASE CLOSURE & CERTIFICATION
+
+V50 is complete.
+
+## V50 production-operations chain
+
+HANDOFF → SUPPORT → INCIDENT → RECOVERY → LEARNING
+
+V50.30 adds one read-only certification surface for both architecture/human-control contracts and current real production evidence.
+
+## Closure hardening discovered during certification
+
+The final clean-baseline regression exposed a nondeterministic ordering edge case in V50.25 corrective-action evidence: verification and completion could be recorded within the same millisecond, allowing `RISK_REDUCTION_VERIFIED` to sort ahead of the newer `COMPLETION_ACCEPTED` state.
+
+V50.30 hardens evidence ordering with deterministic precedence:
+
+1. created timestamp
+2. completion status precedence
+3. record ID tie-break
+
+The full V50 suite was rerun after this fix on a clean exact V50.25 baseline.
+
+## Architecture certification contracts
+
+1. Production Handoff remains human/admin accepted and does not mutate runtime.
+2. Production Health & Support remains human acknowledged/escalated with read-only incident linkage.
+3. Production Incident Command keeps containment, communications, recovery, and resolution human directed.
+4. Production Recovery keeps root cause, corrective work, lessons, and closure human controlled.
+5. Corrective Action Governance keeps execution human owned, verification human recorded, and completion human accepted.
+
+## Certification states
+
+- `V50-CERTIFIED-LIVE`
+  - architecture contracts 5/5
+  - live-state contracts 5/5
+  - corrective actions human-completion accepted
+
+- `V50-ARCHITECTURE-CERTIFIED`
+  - architecture contracts pass
+  - real production lifecycle evidence is still incomplete
+
+- `V50-CERTIFICATION-FAILED`
+  - one or more architecture/human-control contracts fail
+
